# Frontend tests

Colocate tests as `ComponentName.test.tsx` next to the file under test. Use Vitest, Testing Library, and `userEvent`. Test what the analyst sees and does, not implementation details.

- Query by role, label, or text (`getByRole`, `getByLabelText`) — not `container.querySelector`
- Mock `/api` fetches (SWR / `fetch`); do not call the live FastAPI server
- Cover loading, empty, error, and the happy path for each new view or control
- For filters, overrides, and review-queue flags, assert the UI updates after the user action

```tsx
import { render, screen } from "@testing-library/react";
import userEvent from "@testing-library/user-event";

test("filters the queue by untrusted description", async () => {
  const user = userEvent.setup();
  render(<ReviewQueue />);
  await user.click(screen.getByRole("button", { name: /description_untrusted/i }));
  expect(screen.getByText(/611040/)).toBeInTheDocument();
});
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
expect(wrapper.state.flag).toBe("description_untrusted");

// ✅ GOOD
expect(screen.getByRole("status")).toHaveTextContent(/untrusted/i);
```

If Vitest is not configured, add it to `web/` (`vitest`, `jsdom`, `@testing-library/react`, `@testing-library/user-event`, `@testing-library/jest-dom`) and a `test` script. Run `npm test` from `web/` before finishing.
